('finite_extreme',[],B+', '+hr+'∀ x ∈ T, ∃ y ∈ T, (∀ z ∈ T, ¬ R z y) ∧ (y = x ∨ R y x)','Use finite well-foundedness on subtype T: Mathlib Finite.wellFounded_of_trans_of_irrefl (Data/Fintype/Card) with local IsTrans and Std.Irrefl instances. Well-founded induction on the chosen point: if it has an improving predecessor, recurse and compose transitivity; otherwise it is an extreme. Alternatively finite set induction. Only the finite relation is assumed, not an oracle witness.'),
