('nonwinner_strict_dominator',['winning_dominator'],C+', '+hr+f'∀ x ∈ T, feasible x → x ∉ {S}winners T feasible R → ∃ y ∈ {S}winners T feasible R, R y x','The winning_dominator alternative y=x contradicts nonmembership, so retain its strict relation branch. This is the original omitted-record guarantee, including all finite non-total strict orders.'),
('pareto_laws',[],f'∀ (m : ℕ), (∀ a : Fin m → ℤ, ¬ {S}pareto a a) ∧ (∀ a b c : Fin m → ℤ, {S}pareto a b → {S}pareto b c → {S}pareto a c)','Unfold pareto. Irreflexivity follows from the required strict coordinate. For transitivity combine coordinatewise inequalities and reuse a strict coordinate from the first relation with the second weak inequality.'),
('lex_laws',[],f'∀ (m : ℕ), (∀ a : Fin m → ℤ, ¬ {S}lex a a) ∧ (∀ a b c : Fin m → ℤ, {S}lex a b → {S}lex b c → {S}lex a c)','Unfold the explicit first-differing-coordinate lex relation. For two witness indices i,j, split i<j,i=j,j<i; choose the earlier index and use preceding-coordinate equalities. At equal indices compose strict inequalities. Fin order trichotomy works even m=0.'),
('better_laws',['pareto_laws','lex_laws'],f'∀ (m : ℕ) (mode : {S}Mode), (∀ a : Fin m → ℤ, ¬ {S}better mode a a) ∧ (∀ a b c : Fin m → ℤ, {S}better mode a b → {S}better mode b c → {S}better mode a c)','Cases on the concrete mode and use the corresponding accepted laws. These are the actual Pareto/lex objective comparisons in the original selector.'),
('selector_exact',['win_sound_complete','empty_iff','better_laws'],D+f', (∀ x, x ∈ {S}select T feasible objective mode ↔ x ∈ T ∧ feasible x ∧ ∀ y ∈ T, feasible y → ¬ {S}better mode (objective y) (objective x)) ∧ ({S}select T feasible objective mode = ∅ ↔ {S}feasibleSet T feasible = ∅)','Instantiate the generic predicate results with R x y=better mode(objective x)(objective y). Discharge its strict-order hypotheses by better_laws. Final theorem has no free relation-transitivity or oracle-correctness hypothesis.'),
